Apart from your standard equipment you'll want:

4 scrolls of gold detection + either 4 !obooze or a forgotten spell to
confuse yourself.
Confused GD will find traps and portals. Use immediately upon entering
each plane.

2-3 /oDigging for Earth (you'll be getting another as soon as you get
there) or +oDig. I rarely use more than one wand.

As many /oTeleportation as you can be bothered to carry. To chase
air-elementals and the hordes on the Astral Plane. Unless you are
trying something fancy, avoid fighting as much as you can. Remember you
can't teleport away the Riders or their corpses.

/oDeath for Rodney, Famine and Pestilence. Bring all ?oCharging if you
have them, as well as magic markers and blank scrolls to write more. Be
ready to zap around 10 charges all together (conservative estimate,
including misses). Remember that +FoD costs power, the Amulet drains
more power, and dropping/picking up the Amulet costs you valuable
turns.

You want to run through the planes without everyone and his grandmother
catching up with you. Never be burdened. Add an exclamation mark to
that sentence on the Plane of Air. Actually; add two.

/oPolymorph can be fun from inside an air-elemental. I bring one just
in case.

=oLevitation for Air. Keep it on through Water and Fire just in case.
As long as you have reflection and have shock-res (from crowning
perhaps), nothing will vapourise it, and you can happily levitate over
the lava.

Have you genocided water creatures? If not, remember they can drown you
even if you are levitating. /oTeleport here as well. Or Finger them.
Plenty of time on Water, actually. Use it to rest after Air.

For Astral, be satiated. Use anything but death on Death, and watch out
for player-monsters carrying Vorpal Blade. ;) Teleport away everything
else, though you can use the insects as a buffer zone. Again, don't be
burdened. Things get crowded, and you need to take advantage of every
open space.

+Cure Sickness or a blessed unihorn against Pestilence.

Your choice which rider to take first. I usually start in the direction
the RNG lands me.

I also bring /oFire against sliming (never happened to me, but one can
never be too careful) and a /oCold.

I dump all residual scrolls of teleportation on level 1, since the
planes are no-teleport.

Bring as many b!oFH as you can, pluss any other healing potions. You'll
need it. I recently ascended a wishless, genoless monk who managed
barely to stay unburdened, and I think I used 5-8 full healings. The
second altar was correct and I only faced Famine (ran from Death).

For score, I always bring all artifacts I've found, though this has
been touch and go with the weight occasionally. This is just my style
though, and not by any means necessary or even desirable perhaps.
